cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite the version you used."
type: software
title: "LangevinSANS"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
authors:
  - family-names: Adams
    given-names: Michael P.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9269-8087"
abstract: >-
  LangevinSANS is a tested analytical Python implementation of the standard
  equilibrium Langevin model for identical, noninteracting spherical magnetic
  particles. It evaluates field-dependent magnetization and magnetization
  second moments and connects them to magnetic unpolarized and
  polarization-averaged spin-flip small-angle neutron scattering observables
  in perpendicular and parallel scattering geometries.
keywords:
  - Langevin model
  - equilibrium magnetization
  - magnetic small-angle neutron scattering
  - SANS
  - magnetic nanoparticles
  - scientific software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AdamsMP92/LangevinSANS"
